# HackTX Runner

A two-player, webcam-controlled endless runner. One player dodges; the other throws
traps at them. Both control the game with hand gestures in front of one webcam.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173 (add `?novision` to play with the keyboard only).

Contributors and coding agents: read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first.

## Shell progress

Prahalad owns the shell and presentation (`prahalad/` branches).

- Title screen explains both player roles, positions, gestures, and keyboard controls.
- Start and replay support clicks, Enter, and runner jump input. Restart listeners are cleaned up.
- Game-over screen shows score and survival time, with an 800 ms replay guard.
- Camera UI shows startup guidance, player labels, hand readiness, and positioning guidance.
- `?novision` shows keyboard instructions; camera startup failure falls back to keyboard controls.

Validation: formatting, TypeScript, 13 unit tests, and production build passed.
Browser checks covered an 800 × 600 layout, click/Enter/jump-input start, game-over,
and replay. Camera readiness transitions were checked with simulated vision frames.
Live two-player webcam and gesture playtesting remains outstanding.

Known integration issue: the saboteur announces its initial hand before the HUD
subscribes, so the first card is invisible until the next hand update. Coordinate
with the runner/saboteur owners to fix installation order or expose initial state.

Next: HUD clarity and feedback, then live camera playtesting, audio/art, and demo polish.

HUD update: added labeled distance, explicit aim lane, larger cards with selection
labels, empty-hand messaging, and fading attack/hit feedback. Event subscriptions
clean up on scene shutdown. Browser playtesting verified aim changes, card selection,
and attack feedback. Formatting, typecheck, 13 tests, and build passed afterward.
